!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: E3.5 embryo
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = MethylC-Seq: Purified DNA spiked in with 0.1% unmethylated cl857 Sam7 lambda DNA (Promega) was sonicated using the microtube protocol-300 of Covaris S2 (Applied Biosystems). End-repair, dA-tailing and ligation were performed using the NEBNext End Repair Module, dA-Tailing Module and NEB T4 ligase. The adaptor-ligated DNA with insert size larger than 200 bp was selected by gel electrophoresis. Bisulfite conversion was performed using the EZ DNA methylation Gold Kit (Zymo Research) according to the manufacturer’s instructions. The time of 64°C incubation was 2 hr for some libraries. Bisulfite- treated DNA was amplified using ZymoTaq DNA Polymerase or KAPA HiFi HotStart Uracil+ ReadyMix with 14-15 cycles.  Mouse gametes and embryos were collected at minimal volume and frozen. DNA was extracted using QIAamp DNA Mini Kit (QIAGEN) and RNA was isolated using RNeasy Micro Kit (QIAGEN).
!Sample_data_processing = Illumina Casava 1.82 software was used for basecalling.
!Sample_data_processing = Once the sequencing data was obtained from Hiseq-2000, the raw data will be analyzed by the standard combined pipeline in the lab including five steps: 1) finding reads hit by adaptor sequence with a custom pair-wise alignment script, 2) low-quality base trimming by Trimmomatic with default parameters, 3) mapping paired-end methylC-seq reads by Bismark (version 0.7.8) with stringent parameters: -N 1 –X 600, 4) removing duplicates by using Picard program, 5) trimming the overlapped part of paired-end reads from one end.
!Sample_data_processing = Quantification of methylation levels of CpGs: For CpG i, define mi as the number of reads showing methylation over position i (both strands). Define ui as the number of reads showing lack of methylation over CpG i. The methylation level is estimated as mi/(mi + ui), which is an estimate of the probability that CpG i is methylated in a molecule sampled randomly from the cell population. Because CpG methylation is symmetric, mi and ui include observations associated with the cytosines on both strands for the i-thCpG.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Format: bed; content: Methylation level for each CpG site plus 2 columns representing the numbers of Cs and Ts. For strand-specific files, the position of each CpG site is displayed as the C position in Watson strand.
